WHAT WAS TAKEN. Nineteen glyphs, across three modules.

`src/data/transitVehicleIcons.js` draws live French transit vehicles by class
(retrieved 2026-08-31): airport_shuttle, directions_boat, directions_bus,
directions_railway, flight, funicular, local_taxi, monorail, subway, train,
tram, trolley.

`cable_car` was taken on the same date and has since been REMOVED, not merely
left unused: the `aerial` class now draws Maki's `aerialway` instead, for the
legibility reason `src/data/transitVehicleIcons.js` records. Its path data is
gone from this project, so nothing under this notice is claimed for it.

`src/data/sharedMobilityIcons.js` draws shared vehicles by form factor
(retrieved 2026-09-01): pedal_bike, electric_bike, electric_scooter,
electric_moped, directions_car.

`src/data/plantFiliereIcons.js` draws two of the three filières of the EDF
generating fleet (retrieved 2026-09-10 at commit 0cbb08816df0): water_drop for
`hydraulique`, local_fire_department for `thermique`. The third, `nucleaire`,
is Temaki's `cooling_tower_radiation` and carries no claim under this notice —
Material has no nuclear glyph, and its `bolt` says electricity, which is what
all three of them make.

Both are PUNCHED out of a tinted plate through an SVG `<mask>` rather than drawn
as ink: a power station marks a PLACE on a photograph of places, and a bare
silhouette is unfindable below 18 px, which is where more than half this fleet
draws. The transform that fits Material's 960-unit box into a 96-unit plate is a
transform and not a rewrite — the coordinates reach the SVG renderer untouched.

A dam was the obvious drawing for the hydro mark and was REJECTED, not for
legibility but for accuracy: `src/data/edfPowerPlants.js` spends a paragraph of
its header refusing to conflate a barrage with the usine it feeds, and this
project draws those structures as their own layer. A drop says water, which is
the whole of what the filière's name claims.

WHAT WAS CHANGED. Nothing, in the artwork.

Only the single `d` path string of each glyph is vendored, verbatim and
unmodified, into those modules — the surrounding SVG document is not, and the
coordinates are NOT rescaled: all three modules carry Material's own
`0 -960 960 960` viewBox precisely so that this paragraph stays true.

At render time each path is drawn TWICE by this project: once as a wide dark
stroke (a halo, so the glyph stays readable over pale terrain) and once as a
white fill (so Cesium's per-billboard colour multiply can tint it — by vehicle
class in the transit layer, by operator in the shared-mobility one, by filière
in the EDF fleet). The path geometry itself is untouched.

THE PLATE ITSELF IN `plantFiliereIcons.js` IS NOT GOOGLE'S and carries no claim
under this notice: the disc, its ring, and the bare version of both drawn for a
filière EDF has not published before are this project's own geometry.

TWO SHAPES IN `sharedMobilityIcons.js` ARE NOT GOOGLE'S and carry no claim
under this notice: the `other` disc (drawn when a feed does not say what a
vehicle is) and the `station` dock rack, both authored by this project in the
same coordinate box. Material's own `bike_dock` was evaluated for the latter
and rejected on legibility — it renders as a bollard at the size this layer
draws.

Apache-2.0 §6 grants no trademark rights, and none is claimed or exercised
here: no operator's mark appears anywhere in this project's iconography.

