SECOND USE, ADDED 2026-09-09: THE INTERFACE ICON FONT, SUBSETTED.

`public/fonts/material-symbols-outlined-subset.woff2` is Material Symbols
Outlined as a font file, redistributed with this project.

Until now the interface loaded the complete variable font over a `<link>` to
Google Fonts: 323 kB and 4 277 glyphs, on every cold boot, for the 28 this
interface draws. The subset is 4 kB.

Source: https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined
        :opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20,400,0,0&icon_names=<the 28 names>
        retrieved 2026-09-09 by `npm run fonts:build`.

WHAT WAS CHANGED. Nothing in any glyph. The subsetting is performed by Google's
own `css2` endpoint, which serves a font built to order for the requested icon
names — this project does not run a subsetter and does not touch the outlines.
Which names are requested is not a hand-kept list either: it is extracted from
the sources (`scripts/lib/materialSymbolGlyphs.mjs`) and pinned by
`src/materialSymbolsSubset.test.mjs`.

`config/material-symbols-subset.json` records the exact glyph list shipped, and
`config/material-symbols-codepoints.txt` is Google's published codepoint table,
copied unmodified from google/material-design-icons, used to tell an icon name
from an ordinary English word.

Apache-2.0 §4 is satisfied by this notice travelling with the file.
